// module.modulemap: the module map of the CMuJoCo target (apple/UEMAKit, work item
// WI-19 of docs/UEMA_APPLE_PORT_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_2026-11-04.html).
//
// WHAT THIS FILE DOES. It names the one header Swift sees when a file writes
// `import CMuJoCo`: shim.h, beside this file, which includes MuJoCo's umbrella header
// <mujoco/mujoco.h> from the binary target "mujoco" (the MuJoCo 3.3.0 XCFramework that
// apple/scripts/build_mujoco_xcframework.sh writes, work item WI-18). The XCFramework's
// own module map (the stage_headers step of that script) declares `module mujoco`, so
// clang turns the include into an import of module mujoco; `export *` below re-exports
// it ("The wildcard export syntax export * re-exports all of the modules that were
// imported in the actual header file", https://clang.llvm.org/docs/Modules.html, read
// November 4, 2026), so the Swift modules reach mjModel, mjData, mjvScene and the
// functions through this one import.
//
// WHY A CUSTOM MODULE MAP. SwiftPM's ModuleMapGenerator.swift ("First check for a
// custom module map"; the filename constant moduleMapFilename = "module.modulemap";
// read November 4, 2026) uses a module.modulemap found in the public headers folder
// as is. Package.swift gives this target publicHeadersPath ".", so the public headers
// folder is Sources/CMuJoCo itself and this file sits flat beside shim.h and the
// placeholder CMuJoCo.c. Without this file SwiftPM would generate no module map: its
// umbrella-directory rule applies only "if 'PublicHeadersDir' contains only header
// files and no subdirectories", and CMuJoCo.c is in it. SwiftPM's
// TargetSourcesBuilder.swift classifies a .modulemap file under its own rule
// (fileTypes: ["modulemap"]), places it in no source list and emits no diagnostic for
// it (read November 4, 2026).
//
// NO link DECLARATION. The static library is linked because Package.swift names the
// binary target "mujoco" as this target's dependency; a `link "mujoco"` line here
// would add an autolink entry that needs a library search path this package does not
// set, so it is left out.
//
// Grammar used (https://clang.llvm.org/docs/Modules.html, "Module Map Language"):
// module-declaration `module` module-id '{' module-member* '}'; header-declaration
// `header` string-literal; export-declaration `export` wildcard-module-id.
//
// CHECK RUN HERE (Windows, November 4, 2026; no Swift toolchain): clang 20.1.8 parsed
// this file with -fmodules -fimplicit-module-maps for the target
// arm64-apple-macosx14.0 against the 14 headers of tag 3.3.0 staged as the script
// stages them; the test files under Tests/CMuJoCoTests state the commands.
module CMuJoCo {
  header "shim.h"
  export *
}
